SUMMARY:AI Training Day at All Things Open: Three All-Day AI Workshops
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nWant to actually learn AI\, hands on\, i
 n one day? All Things AI is heading to All Things Open in downtown Raleigh
  for a full day of AI training. Pick one of three all-day workshops\, brin
 g a laptop\, and leave with something working.\n\nJoin Mark Hinkle\, All T
 hings AI Co-founder for his Vibecoding workshop for non-coders he'll show 
 you how to use agents to make something awesome. Or Don Shin and John Will
 is doing a repeat of All Things AI's workshop day with new updates.\n\nRSV
 P here so we know you're coming\, then register for your workshop at All T
 hings Open. Members of this community get 25% off: **[register with the Al
 l Things AI 25% discount](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1990317243453/?disc
 ount=AllThingsAI25).**\n\n**Pick your workshop (Monday\, October 19\, 9:00
  AM to 5:30 PM\, doors open at 7:30 AM)**\n\n* **[AI Agents & Vibe Coding]
 (https://2026.allthingsopen.org/ai-agents-vibe-coding)** with **Mark Hinkl
 e** (Peripety Labs\, co-founder of All Things AI). Build and deploy a real
  application with AI agents\, and leave with a working app and a GitHub re
 pository that documents every change the agents made. No coding experience
  needed. Bring a laptop\, free GitHub and Vercel accounts\, and an idea yo
 u want to build.\n* **[AI Agents in Production](https://2026.allthingsopen
 .org/ai-agents-model-context-protocol-mcp)** with **Don Shin** (Founder an
 d CEO\, CrossComm). Agent fundamentals\, production patterns (ReAct\, loop
 s\, graphs\, multi-agent orchestration)\, security and observability\, plu
 s tokenomics and small language models. Bring a laptop and a paid Claude s
 ubscription. API and command-line familiarity helps.\n* **[AI for DevSecOp
 s](https://2026.allthingsopen.org/ai-for-devsecops)** with **John Willis**
  (AI CIO). Where AI strengthens security across the delivery lifecycle\, c
 ontrols for AI-assisted work\, and a concrete plan for your next AI-enable
 d DevSecOps initiative. For people who know source control\, CI/CD and com
 mon security practices. No AI background required. Bring a laptop.\n*\n\n*
 *What's included:** the all-day workshop\, admission to Tuesday\, October 
 20 (keynotes and 100+ sessions\, including more than 40 AI sessions)\, box
 ed lunches and networking.\n\n**Pricing:** $299 through Friday\, October 9
 \, then $399. Take 25% off either price with the [All Things AI link](http
 s://www.eventbrite.com/e/1990317243453/?discount=AllThingsAI25).\n\nMost e
 mployers cover this as professional development.\n\n**More AI at All Thing
 s Open**\n\n* Monday 2-hour AI Deep Dive sessions (agent security\, voice 
 agents\, Claude\, open source agentic systems): $149 Monday pass\n* Free M
 onday co-located events: an [AI hackathon](https://2026.allthingsopen.org/
 major-league-hacking) for all skill levels\, [Inclusion & Diversity in Ope
 n Source](https://2026.allthingsopen.org/inclusion-diversity-in-open-sourc
 e)\, the [Open Source Accessibility Summit](https://2026.allthingsopen.org
 /open-source-accessibility-summit) and the Community Leadership Summit\n* 
 Students and people underrepresented in tech: [scholarships and discounts]
 (https://2026.allthingsopen.org/scholarships-discounts)\n\n**Full AI lineu
 p: [2026.allthingsopen.org/ai](https://2026.allthingsopen.org/ai)**\n\nHos
 ted by Mark Hinkle and Todd Lewis\, co-founders of All Things AI.
